# "net-nomemcg": the "net" kernel WITHOUT the memory controller (CONFIG_MEMCG); candidate fix for the OOM-kill hang of net/netfilter (docs/KERNEL-BUILD.md, "OOM hang investigation"). Otherwise as net.config; merged after kw_defconfig (and kw_smp.config) for BOTH the UP and SMP kernel.
# Based on the gregbell/linux-wasm-unk8s fork's commit 17450909 (GPL-2.0), with our additions; reasoning there.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-cpw-net-nomemcg"

# containers: cgroup v2 controllers (memory, cpu incl. cpu.max, cpuset)
CONFIG_CGROUP_SCHED=y
CONFIG_FAIR_GROUP_SCHED=y
CONFIG_CFS_BANDWIDTH=y
# needs patches/linux/0001 (relaxes `depends on SMP`)
CONFIG_CPUSETS=y

# runc/crun device-cgroup eBPF program
CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y
CONFIG_CGROUP_BPF=y
# keyrings (runc session keyring, kubelet's /proc/sys/kernel/keys)
CONFIG_KEYS=y

# L2 networking: veth is already on upstream; bridge new. IGMP snooping off (extra call depth, unused).
CONFIG_VETH=y
CONFIG_BRIDGE=y
# CONFIG_BRIDGE_IGMP_SNOOPING is not set
